TEXT -352 -320 Left 2 ;Increase the load to 150MW
TEXT -680 -280 Left 2 ;This model has the transformer, the generator switch, the speed controller and the AVR inside
TEXT -536 -256 Left 2 ;BlockStart at t=Null with 1500 turns/min (50Hz)\nAfter about 1200ms the nominal voltage is reached\nThe speed regulator is on at startup\nThe AVR(automatic voltage regulator) is off\nThe field-voltage is from a fix pwl source (UEfix=600V=UE0)\nAfter 1200ms the block is switched to the net (t_sync)\nAfter 1200ms the fixed torque is switched on (t_start_fixm)\nAfter 1250ms the speed controller is off (t_stop_nreg)\nThe torque is now entered by a fix pwl source (Block Power output 150MW)\n        Power=Torque*314.159/2 (f=50Hz,p=2)\n        Frequency=1500/60/2 (Umin->Usec,p=2)\n \nAfter 5s the voltagemeasurement of the AVR is on (t_enablev_avr)\nAfter 5.5s the AVR is enabled (t_enable_avr) should be appr. 500ms after voltagemeas is on\n        because now the voltage is settled and the controller can work\nAfter 5.5s the AVR is switched on (t_start_avr)\nAfter 5.6s the fixed field voltage is off (t_stop_fixerr)\nAfter 12s the load is increased to 150MW now the voltage source\n         gets less and less power from the generator
TEXT -1032 -536 Left 5 ;Control-Switchers of the generator:
TEXT -680 -288 Left 2 ;GEN_400MW_20kV_400kV_with_transformer_and_control
TEXT -824 -184 Left 2 ;NOTE: The torquecontrol from the turbine is assumed simple/ideal \nthat mean there is no time constant or limit present\nThis may go for a hydraulic turbine but not for a thermal block
TEXT -992 -624 Left 5 ;This example shows a synchronous generator with Transformer and Controls inside\nThe generators behaviour is controlled only via switchers\nand maybe with external pwl sources at F1 pin (External Exciter voltage) and M pin (external Torque)
